    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Bandits rely on the threat of violence to take whatever they want; they include gang members, outlaws, and mercenaries with no regard for the law. Not every bandit is driven by greed, though: some turn to crime because of unfair laws, desperation, or the threats of ruthless bosses. Bandit crime lords pull the strings of secret organizations and value their own survival above any single henchman or scheme.</p>",
